{"type":"event","event":{"type":"tool_completed","toolCallId":"read_file_2_3ef9888f","toolName":"read_file","result":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 113 lines\n1: Completed-GMT: 2026-10-16 13:22:29 GMT\n2: Completed-Local: 2026-10-16 20:22:29 +07\n3: Coding-Agent: claude\n4: Session-ID: dc3e4b88-02d8-428d-b938-541541f0fbe1\n5: # Slice 6d-a round 2 (continued): opus takeover, finished on codex's partial diff\n6: \n7: Role: VM Runtime. Branch `srvm-6d-a`, base `b9103797`, worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-6d-a`. Model: claude-opus-5-5. Nothing was committed, pushed, or merged. No `src/yang` or `test/yang` file was touched. No collab file is staged. Fable's diff-confirm and sign-off remain outstanding.\n8: \n9: ## What I found on takeover\n10: \n11: Codex's round-2 turn got further than its round-1 report says. When its quota cut it off, it had already:\n12: - regenerated the ledger golden and written the inventory;\n13: - applied the layout-gate ruling, so `static-layouts-at-every-pc` was 1783/0;\n14: - added most of the item 1–13 tests;\n15: - run a 19-mutant implementation-weakening campaign;\n16: - partly audited the docs.\n17: \n18: My first focused run (`target/6da/r3-focused-0.log`: 203 tests, 23,371 assertions) had exactly **one** failure: row 20's pin `[{:pc 0 :obligations #{s}}]`. The measurement gave three leading excluded boundaries. The slow tier had never completed, the per-case counts were printed but not pinned, and two driver coverage classes were never reached.\n19: \n20: ## ATTRIBUTION\n21: \n22: | Authored by | Files / hunks |\n23: |---|---|\n24: | **codex gpt-6.1-sol (inherited, unchanged by me)** | All of `src/cljc/yin/vm/{engine,semantic}.cljc`, `semantic/{frame,layout}.cljc`, `ucf/rows.cljc`; all of `test/yin/vm/{engine_test,malformed_rows}.cljc`, `semantic/{frame_test,layout_test,vm_test}.cljc`, `ucf/{rows_test,rows_custody_test}.cljc`; both fixtures `test/resources/yin/vm/ucf/{rows-checkpoint-v3,ledger-v2}.txt`; `docs/agents/known-gaps.md`, `yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md`, `yin.vm.semantic.md`, `yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md`, `yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md`; every `safepoint_harness_test.cljc` hunk not listed below; the codex part of the docs listed below; every `target/6da/r1-*`/`r2-*` artifact |\n25: | **opus (this turn)** | `safepoint_harness_test.cljc`: (a) the row-20 pin now carries the measured `[pc 0, 1, 2] × #{s}`; (b) a new general check: obligations are unanswered at each excluded boundary and answered at the first measured one; (c) `boundary-description` `:store-keys` also counts installing modules' exports, matching `rows/discharge!`'s answer order (the duplicate key was removed); (d) `quick-boundary-pins`, `quick-boundary-coverage` and their assertions in `sampled-returned-boundaries`; (e) new `running-beside-a-reader`, `two-woken-callers`, `product-driver-cases` and `product-returned-boundaries`; (f) the 89-case pin table and coverage assertion in the slow `every-returned-boundary`; (g) `fn [i p]` → `fn [i _p]` in `structural-sample` (kondo warning) |\n26: | opus | docs: `yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md` §9 \"refuse unless quiescent\" → holds; `yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md` §7.6.3 amended marker on \"ready-queue must be empty at lift\"; `yin.vm.dependency-completion.md` §7 amended marker on the `:ready-queue must be empty` clause |\n27: | opus | `target/6da/r3-*` evidence (logs, measurements, `r3-mutants-test.clj`, `r3-mutation-results.edn`) and this report |\n28: \n29: Still flagged for Fable's diff-confirm: the retained-FFI fixture carries the actual wait entry's `:call-id` (`:parked-0`), not nil. This is codex's correction and I kept it.\n30: \n31: ## What I STOPPED on\n32: \n33: Nothing. One deviation from a ruling's literal text, resolved under \"carry the actual value and record it\":\n34: \n35: - **Row 20's excluded set is 3 boundaries, not 1.** Ruling 2 says \"row 20's excluded set is exactly `[S₀, obligations #{s}]`\". Measured, the setup batch's first `s/def!` stores `s` only after pcs 0, 1 and 2. All three boundaries refuse `[:yin.k/unsatisfied :incomplete]` with obligations exactly `#{s}` and zero serves. They form a contiguous leading run, and every later boundary lifts. That is the ruling's general rule and acceptance item 7's own criterion (\"lifts only from the first boundary at which its definitions are answered in the store\").\n36:   - The pre-existing `conservative-prefixes-refuse-before-serving` test (codex) pins the same three prefixes independently.\n37:   - My new assertions prove the cause: `s` is absent at each excluded boundary and present at the first measured one.\n38:   - `discharge!` is unchanged.\n39:   - Item 7's doc text keeps the ruling's verbatim \"the leading boundary\" wording. **Fable/acting Architect: confirm or re-word.**\n40: - **Row 17 is a \"like case\".** Excluded runs, all with obligation `#{host.mod/f}`, answered once the `require` of `host.mod` installs: bare 16, operand 18, depth-3 31, captured 43. Note that in row 17 captured, excluded boundaries (43) outnumber measured ones (27). The obligation is defined by the module the case's own program requires, not by a store `def!`. I count that as \"names the case's own program defines later\" (the work order: \"row 20 and any like case\"). Flagged for confirmation.\n41: \n42: ## Acceptance 1–14: final outcome\n43: \n44: Per-var counters come from the final tree (`target/6da/r3-per-var.log`). Pass/fail/error; no var has any failure or error.\n45: \n46: | # | Outcome | Evidence (pass counts) |\n47: |---|---|---|\n48: | 1 | Done | `frame-test/run-state-rules` 13, `worked-example-running-inventory` 48, `delivery-and-running-windows-are-distinct` 5 |\n49: | 2 | Done | `rows-test/run-row-slot-and-reference-kinds` 5, `completion-outcome-slot-matrix` 84, `completion-try-and-update-refusals` 16, `task-products-and-ready-validation` 36, `ready-site-mismatch-and-halted-product` 6, `completed-put-history-and-shape-only-ids` 20; all lower refusals assert zero attaches. Mutant campaign below. |\n50: | 3 | Done | `illegal-task-product-matrix` 30, `running-task-round-trip-and-fencing` 32, `halted-with-outstanding-waits-is-normalized-separately` 8, `a-nonempty-ready-queue-is-carried` 4 |\n51: | 4 | Done | `completed-link-and-install-outcomes` 48, `completed-link-request-and-active-completions` 32 (zero appends: the retired envelope is never re-appended) |\n52: | 5 | Done | `shared-cursor-independent-continuations` 9 (independent source vs receiver continuation equality, ordered update bodies), plus the update-body case in `ready-value-portability-and-independent-update-body` 8 |\n53: | 6 | Done | `rows-custody-test/exclusive-completed-write-is-history` 10, `terminal-completed-write-raises-the-same-outcome` 21 (identity-normalized diagnostic), `completed-ffi-append-becomes-a-response-wait` 8, `completed-poll-observation-is-an-ordinary-read-outcome` 7 |\n54: | 7 | Done (JVM) | Quick: `sampled-returned-boundaries` **13,755** (23 cases; per-case `[measured excluded park halt]` and coverage pinned). `product-returned-boundaries` **850** (driver from constructed starts; reaches `:active-plus-waits` and `:active-plus-ready`, which no corpus row reaches). Slow: `every-returned-boundary`, 89 cases, per-case counts pinned: **129,274 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors** on the final tree (`r3-slow-final.log`; the measurement run `r3-slow-measure.log` predates the pins). Per point: lift, lower into an isolated world, immediate relift equality (law 2), law 6, window tampers (`check-window-tampers`), isolated law-1 continuation to the reference. Leading exclusions: see STOPPED. |\n55: | 8 | Done | Structural sampler (5 named samples) across all 22 bare rows plus unwrapped row 20; every boundary for rows 1 and 20 and for the products; `pre-branch-ghost-is-conservatively-unsatisfied` 4; existing cursor/capture/nil/hold cases still green in the quick tier |\n56: | 9 | Done | `layout-test/static-layouts-at