aseline 1,988/0/0):\n67: \n68: | Mutant | Fail / error |\n69: |---|---|\n70: | ready roots skipped by `lower-defect` | 15 fail |\n71: | run-fuel restarts execution after a bridge result | 52 fail |\n72: | children run unbudgeted (`vm/run`) in the fuel round | 11 fail |\n73: | dispatch on `active-continuation?` instead of control presence | 1 fail + 1 error |\n74: \n75: ## Ledger golden regeneration (ruling 3)\n76: \n77: - Regenerated by codex through `ledger-fixtures/render` only (`target/6da/r2-ledger-render.log`).\n78: - Field-classified old/new inventory: **`target/6da/r2-ledger-diff-inventory.edn`**. Classification `:address-only`.\n79: - The six frame-byte equalities are journal frames 2, 9, 11, 13, 14 and 15. Every change sits at a `:segment/blake3-…` path (`:datoms i 2` or `:datoms i 2 :yin.k/root`); the 14 other frames are byte-identical.\n80: - I independently checked the git diff: exactly lines 2 (projection) and 5, 12, 14, 16, 17, 18 (= frames 2, 9, 11, 13–15) changed. No continuation frame pack's own bytes changed.\n81: - Digests (codex-recorded): projection `419e3aa6…` → `52f8127f…`; golden BLAKE3 `5de18ed0…` → `59a6944d…`. Full values are in the inventory file. I did not recompute the golden BLAKE3.\n82: - Other re-mints (codex, authorized): rows-checkpoint 52/53 addresses (`fixture-remints.json`); 19 inline task-root pins (`root-remints.txt`).\n83: \n84: ## Docs audit (item 14)\n85: \n86: I re-ran the inventory greps (`safepoint|not-quiescent|Quiesce|quiescent`, kind lists, context lists, `maybe-run`, one-cycle). I amended three remaining normative stale clauses, listed in ATTRIBUTION. Codex's `:running` kind in the tuples kind list was already present.\n87: \n88: Deliberately left as-is:\n89: - **UCF §7.7.4 \"Quiesce\" step 1 and §7.8 lifecycle step 1.** Plan v2.1 §3.8 and 6d-b item 8 assign them to 6d-b.\n90: - **UCF version-0/1 body map `:blocked | :parked | :halted`** and **v2-amendment's version-2 body map.** These are historical wire versions.\n91: - **UCF acceptance text \"queued work gives not-quiescent\"** and **continuation §8 phase-6 acceptance lists.** These are historical slice records.\n92: - **`yin.vm.linker.dht.md` mention of not-quiescent.** Linker-DHT hunks are out of this slice, as in round 1.\n93: - **`ffi/maybe-run` mentions.** These describe the unchanged unrestricted `vm/run`.\n94: \n95: The plan v2.1 §3.8 checks hold: no normative clause assigns the guard to 6d-b, forbids completed link/install wakes, validates completed installs against live installs, restarts fuel through `maybe-run`, or promises one-cycle hold resolution. The §3.5 dead-ambient sentence and the item 7/9 ruling text are in `yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md`.\n96: \n97: ## File-to-commit mapping (proposal; nothing committed)\n98: \n99: | Commit group | Files |\n100: |---|---|\n101: | Runtime/carrier | `src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc`, `semantic.cljc`, `semantic/frame.cljc`, `semantic/layout.cljc`, `ucf/rows.cljc` |\n102: | Tests and re-minted fixtures | `test/yin/vm/engine_test.cljc`, `malformed_rows.cljc`, `semantic/{frame,layout,safepoint_harness,vm}_test.cljc`, `ucf/{rows,rows_custody}_test.cljc`, `test/resources/yin/vm/ucf/rows-checkpoint-v3.txt`, `test/resources/yin/vm/ucf/ledger-v2.txt` |\n103: | Docs | `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md`, `yin.vm.semantic.md`, `yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md`, `yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md`, `yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md`, `yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md`, `yin.vm.dependency-completion.md`, `docs/agents/known-gaps.md` |\n104: | Never commit | all `collab/` files (prompts, reports), `target/6da/*` |\n105: \n106: ## Skipped / not claimed\n107: \n108: - Node, Dart and the three-host slow landing run were not executed (orchestrator's lanes).\n109: - I did not re-run codex's 19-mutant campaign. Its `src` and test inputs are unchanged since it ran.\n110: - I did not recompute the golden BLAKE3 digests.\n111: - Every inherited codex hunk is unreviewed by 