oday. The latter is an existing carrier normalization, not a claim that the source halt value is unobservable; acceptance pins it separately.\n173: +\n174: +\n175:  ### 2.7 The bijection with the keyed frame\n176:  \n177:  **PROPOSED.** `rows->frame` and `frame->rows` (`yin.vm.ucf.rows`, §8.1)\n178: @@ -432,10 +486,10 @@ return-frame sites, `K` structure, pending compatibility). **PROPOSED**\n179:  (frame/defect frame code context task)\n180:  ;; frame   : a decoded canonical frame (§1.2), any shape (the rules judge it)\n181:  ;; code    : {A vector}, every vector already code/well-formed? (step 4 of the carrier ran)\n182: -;; context : :wait | :captured | :parked\n183: +;; context : :wait | :captured | :parked | :running | :ready\n184:  ;; task    : decoded task context, plain data, no engine:\n185:  ;;           {:parked-key P-or-nil                 ; the parked-table key this frame sits under (:parked only)\n186: -;;            :ffi-call-ids #{…}                   ; call ids of the task's live :ffi and :ffi-request pendings\n187: +;;            :ffi-call-ids #{…}                   ; call ids of the task's outstanding and completed FFI call ids\n188:  ;;            :free-env {sym V …}}                 ; the root's free environment, decoded\n189:  ;; => nil, or {:yin.k/kind k :yin.k/path p …}\n190:  \n191: @@ -469,7 +523,7 @@ body `b` as phase-5 §1.2 (closure pcs innermost first) and `params(c) =\n192:  \n193:  | # | Rule | Kind |\n194:  |---|---|---|\n195: -| S1 | `frame` is a map; `:yin.k/state` is `:act` or `:tail`; an `act` has exactly the keys `:yin.k/state :yin.k/segment :yin.k/pc :yin.k/env :yin.k/window :yin.k/deliver :yin.k/k` plus optionally `:yin.k/pending`; a `tail` exactly `:yin.k/state :yin.k/segment :yin.k/site :yin.k/deliver :yin.k/k` plus optionally `:yin.k/pending` | `:frame-shape` |\n196: +| S1 | States are `:act`, `:tail`, `:run`; a run has exactly state, segment, pc, env, window and k. Delivery states keep their existing exact key sets. | `:fra