 |\n727:  |---|---|---|---|\n728: -| root | blocked / parked | exclusive | `{:yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive :yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/next-op-seq}` plus `:yin.k/origin` on every successor, absent on a first export |\n729: -| root | blocked / parked | fork | nil |\n730: +| root | running / blocked / parked | exclusive | `{:yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive :yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/next-op-seq}` plus `:yin.k/origin` on every successor, absent on a first export |\n731: +| root | running / blocked / parked | fork | nil |\n732:  | root | halted | exclusive | `{:yin.k/origin …}` only: a result is not a lease subject |\n733:  | root | halted | fork | nil: a fork halt has no custody data and a first fork halt has no origin to carry |\n734:  | child | any | — | nil; validated with its root's occurrence, origin and counter passed down |\n735: @@ -503,6 +497,37 @@ plain data in the root rather than a row kind: each instruction vector\n736:  keeps its own address `A` computed exactly as UCF §7.3.2 computes it, and\n737:  the carrier verifies, never recomputes, that address.\n738:  \n739: +**Amended 2026-10-16 (any-pc, owner invariant 2026-10-17)**\n740: +\n741: +| Kind | Machine classification | Waits | Run | Ready | Parked-id | Result |\n742: +|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---|\n743: +| `:running` | `:control` set | 0..n | exactly one | 0..n | absent | absent |\n744: +| `:parked` | control nil; value names a held parked record | 0..n | none | 0..n | table key | absent |\n745: +| `:blocked` | control nil; not parked; waits or ready nonempty | 0..n | none | 0..n | absent | absent |\n746: +| `:halted` | control nil; halted; waits and ready empty | none | none | none | absent | present |\n747: +\n748: +A halted activation beside queued work classifies `:blocked`: the scheduler processes the queue before returning the halt result. A halted activation with outstanding waits and an empty queue also classifies `:blocked`, dropping its halt value as today