3 (custody/lifecycle) includes stage-local retention text + closed-gate entries text ✓.\n\nNow potential issue (b): **run-fuel in semantic.cljc uses `(code/reg? n)`** — but what namespace alias? The ns require list at the top of semantic.cljc — diff line 1090-1096 shows the ns form beginning; `code` isn't in the visible requires ([dao.jing :as jing] [dao.stream.apply :as apply2] [yin.vm :as vm] ...). Need to check the worktree.\n\nAlso `(ffi/installed? v)` needs `[yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]`.\n\nAnd `(engine/scheduler-round-fuel machine register-restore #(run-fuel % n))` — register-restore is defined above in semantic.cljc ✓ (line 1097 area).\n\nLet me now read the key worktree files to verify these details. Also I want to check `vm-hot*`'s handling when control is nil (scheduler fallback): \n\n```clojure\n(defn- vm-hot*\n  \"Execute fuel instructions with the activation in locals; nil fuel runs to exit.\"\n  [machine fuel]\n  (if (and (nil? (:control machine)) (nil? (:k machine)))\n    (machine- ... )))\n```\nThe diff only shows the signature change (defn vm-hot → defn- vm-hot*), body unchanged. The old vm-hot had a scheduler fallback? v2.1: \"Therefore no run-fuel path falls through vm-hot into its unbudgeted scheduler fallback.\" — the old vm-hot when control nil and k nil → returns machine? or runs scheduler? The spec's verified site says \"semantic.cljc:137 | Hot-loop fallback, scheduler wrapper and public protocol execution paths.\" Let me read vm-hot* body in the worktree.\n\nThen: **run-fuel with control nil and k non-nil?** Interesting: vm-hot* checks `(and (nil? control) (nil? k))`. run-fuel dispatches on `(some? (:control machine))`. If control is nil but k is non-nil... can that happen? A restored machine has :control nil :k nil for blocked. A resumed tail state has control set? Hmm, a tail state resumes through K... In the semantic machine, control is the run state; after a tail call parks, what's control? Probably still {:segment :pc}. OK.\n\nLet me read sema